WEBVTT

00:00:20.452 --> 00:00:22.484
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.378
Sammy!

00:00:24.117 --> 00:00:26.088
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:26.111 --> 00:00:26.674
Go!

00:00:30.393 --> 00:00:31.601
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:33.686
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:37.521 --> 00:00:40.923
This is dad's book. I think dad
wants us to pick up where he left off.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.876
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:42.891 --> 00:00:45.519
Family business. Do you think
Mom wanted all this for us?

00:00:45.534 --> 00:00:46.645
I can't do this alone.

00:00:47.412 --> 00:00:48.163
I'm driving.

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:22.416
Man, these are some phat houses, huh?

00:01:22.792 --> 00:01:23.923
I'd like to live here.

00:01:24.261 --> 00:01:24.599
Yeah.

00:01:25.162 --> 00:01:26.708
Too bad you can't afford it.

00:01:27.662 --> 00:01:28.837
Yeah, you're right.

00:01:29.512 --> 00:01:31.850
This neighborhood will be
damn expensive when it's done.

00:01:56.628 --> 00:01:57.899
This place is perfect...

00:01:58.475 --> 00:01:58.903
Ow!

00:02:00.097 --> 00:02:01.283
...Except for the mosquitoes.

00:02:05.349 --> 00:02:06.100
Aah!

00:02:07.264 --> 00:02:07.744
Dustin?

00:02:08.849 --> 00:02:10.183
Help me, I'm trapped!

00:02:11.135 --> 00:02:12.416
I broke my ankle.

00:02:13.969 --> 00:02:14.991
I'll get a rope!

00:02:17.659 --> 00:02:18.537
Oh, damn.

00:02:35.709 --> 00:02:36.664
Oh god!

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:48.749
Travis, help!

00:02:48.911 --> 00:02:49.710
Hang on!

00:03:00.035 --> 00:03:01.513
Travis, help!

00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:03.775
Aah! Aaah!

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:05.525
It's okay, Dustin. It's okay.

00:03:08.964 --> 00:03:09.517
Dustin?

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:11.907
Dustin, I'm here.

00:03:14.182 --> 00:03:14.945
Oh, god.

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.603
<i>I got something to say.</i>

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:41.936
<i>Ow!</i>

00:03:44.452 --> 00:03:45.648
<i>Yeah, you're doing all right.</i>

00:03:45.664 --> 00:03:47.282
<i>Gonna start a fire</i>

00:03:50.558 --> 00:03:52.478
You know, we could get
day jobs once in a while.

00:03:53.342 --> 00:03:54.468
Hunting's our day job,

00:03:54.984 --> 00:03:56.110
And the pay is crap.

00:03:56.357 --> 00:03:57.518
Yeah, but hustling pool,

00:03:58.254 --> 00:03:59.158
Credit-Card scams?

00:03:59.842 --> 00:04:01.513
It's not the most honest
thing in the world, Dean.

00:04:01.743 --> 00:04:02.804
Well, let's see... Honest...

00:04:03.795 --> 00:04:04.506
Fun and easy...

00:04:05.964 --> 00:04:06.879
It's no contest.

00:04:07.075 --> 00:04:07.484
Besides,

00:04:08.055 --> 00:04:09.404
We're good at it. It's
what we were raised to do.

00:04:09.473 --> 00:04:12.284
How we were raised was
jacked. Yeah, says you.

00:04:12.717 --> 00:04:14.328
We got a new gig or what? Maybe.

00:04:14.568 --> 00:04:17.203
Oasis Plains, Oklahoma.
Not far from here.

00:04:17.498 --> 00:04:18.856
Gas-Company employee.

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:21.362
Dustin Burwash,

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.907
Supposedly died from creutzfeldt-Jakob.

00:04:24.244 --> 00:04:24.584
Huh?

00:04:25.229 --> 00:04:27.399
Human mad cow disease. Mad cow?

00:04:28.525 --> 00:04:29.856
Wasn't that on "Oprah"?

00:04:30.402 --> 00:04:31.428
You watch "Oprah"?

00:04:34.713 --> 00:04:37.531
So this guy eats a bad burger.
Why is it our kind of thing?

00:04:38.748 --> 00:04:41.528
Mad cow disease causes
massive brain degeneration.

00:04:41.531 --> 00:04:43.998
It takes months, even years
for the damage to appear,

00:04:44.004 --> 00:04:45.188
But this guy, Dustin,

00:04:45.376 --> 00:04:47.994
Sounds like his brain
disintegrated in about an hour,

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:49.258
Maybe less.

00:04:49.275 --> 00:04:50.748
Okay, that's weird. Yeah.

00:04:51.217 --> 00:04:52.523
Now, it could be a disease,

00:04:53.184 --> 00:04:54.710
Or it could be something much nastier.

00:04:55.658 --> 00:04:57.301
All right, Oklahoma.

00:04:57.947 --> 00:04:59.429
Man, work, work, work.

00:05:00.339 --> 00:05:01.733
No time to spend my money.

00:05:02.862 --> 00:05:06.770
<i>We got the power, we got the glory</i>

00:05:06.954 --> 00:05:09.020
<i>Just say you need it...</i>

00:05:16.851 --> 00:05:17.802
Travis Weaver?

00:05:19.561 --> 00:05:20.358
Yeah, that's right.

00:05:21.715 --> 00:05:23.756
Are you the Travis who
worked with uncle Dusty?

00:05:24.776 --> 00:05:26.489
Dustin never mentioned nephews.

00:05:27.052 --> 00:05:27.650
Really?

00:05:28.108 --> 00:05:29.316
Well, he sure mentioned you.

00:05:29.363 --> 00:05:30.829
He said you were the greatest.

00:05:31.275 --> 00:05:32.037
Oh, he did?

00:05:32.525 --> 00:05:33.182
Huh.

00:05:33.898 --> 00:05:35.681
So, we wanted to ask you...

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.417
What exactly happened out there?

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:39.693
I'm not sure.

00:05:40.168 --> 00:05:42.866
He fell in the sinkhole. I went
to the truck to get some rope, and

00:05:43.382 --> 00:05:44.696
By the time I got back...

00:05:45.412 --> 00:05:46.620
What'd you see?

00:05:48.145 --> 00:05:48.591
Nothing.

00:05:49.313 --> 00:05:50.052
Just Dustin.

00:05:50.134 --> 00:05:51.870
No wounds or anything?

00:05:52.316 --> 00:05:53.231
Well, he was bleeding

00:05:53.442 --> 00:05:55.846
From his eyes and his ears, his nose,

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:57.242
That's it.

00:05:57.876 --> 00:05:59.670
So do you think it could
be this whole mad cow thing?

00:06:01.366 --> 00:06:02.035
I don't know.

00:06:02.645 --> 00:06:03.853
That's what the doctors are saying.

00:06:03.923 --> 00:06:04.827
But if it was,

00:06:05.472 --> 00:06:09.824
He would have acted strange beforehand,
like dementia, loss of motor control.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.821
You ever notice anything like that? No.

00:06:12.199 --> 00:06:12.752
No way.

00:06:14.002 --> 00:06:16.316
Yeah, but if it wasn't some
disease, what the hell was it?

00:06:17.517 --> 00:06:18.395
That's a good question.

00:06:18.599 --> 00:06:18.972
Yep.

00:06:19.182 --> 00:06:20.595
Can you tell us where this happened?

00:06:21.361 --> 00:06:21.751
Yeah.

00:06:45.568 --> 00:06:46.024
Huh.

00:06:47.575 --> 00:06:48.296
What do you think?

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:50.002
I don't know,

00:06:50.017 --> 00:06:52.607
But if that guy Travis was right,
it happened pretty damn fast.

00:06:53.389 --> 00:06:54.200
So what?

00:06:54.523 --> 00:06:56.175
Some sort of creature
chewed on his brain?

00:06:56.198 --> 00:06:57.625
No, there'd be an entry wound.

00:06:58.046 --> 00:06:59.744
Sounds like this thing
worked from the inside.

00:07:03.579 --> 00:07:04.105
Huh.

00:07:05.232 --> 00:07:07.088
It looks like there's only room for one.

00:07:07.899 --> 00:07:08.966
You want to flip a coin?

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:12.240
Dean, we have no idea what's down there.

00:07:13.773 --> 00:07:15.268
All right, I'll go if you're scared.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:16.551
Scared?

00:07:16.956 --> 00:07:18.068
Flip the damn coin.

00:07:21.767 --> 00:07:22.563
Call it in the air...

00:07:22.826 --> 00:07:23.405
Chicken.

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:26.034
I'm going.

00:07:26.102 --> 00:07:27.011
I said I'd go.

00:07:27.324 --> 00:07:28.333
I'm going.

00:07:28.752 --> 00:07:29.600
All right.

00:07:31.509 --> 00:07:32.858
Don't drop me.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:39.107
So, you found some beetles

00:07:39.212 --> 00:07:40.550
In a hole in the ground.

00:07:41.429 --> 00:07:42.860
That's shocking, Sam.

00:07:43.388 --> 00:07:45.429
There were no tunnels, no tracks,

00:07:45.852 --> 00:07:48.385
No evidence of any other
kind of creature down there.

00:07:48.635 --> 00:07:50.386
You know, some beetles do eat meat.

00:07:50.405 --> 00:07:53.192
Now, it's usually dead meat, but...
How many did you find down there?

00:07:53.464 --> 00:07:53.924
10.

00:07:55.365 --> 00:07:57.730
It would take a whole lot more than
that to eat out somebody's brain.

00:07:57.843 --> 00:07:59.063
Well, maybe there were more.

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:01.502
I don't know. It sounds
like a stretch to me.

00:08:01.524 --> 00:08:04.362
We need more information on
the area, the neighborhood,

00:08:04.386 --> 00:08:07.025
Whether something like this
has ever happened before.

00:08:09.007 --> 00:08:09.524
What?

00:08:10.239 --> 00:08:11.588
I know a good place to start.

00:08:13.154 --> 00:08:15.429
I'm kind of hungry for a
little barbecue, how about you?

00:08:18.045 --> 00:08:19.652
What, we can't talk to the locals?

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:22.874
And the free food's got nothing to do
with it? Of course not. I'm a professional.

00:08:23.456 --> 00:08:23.953
Right.

00:08:43.913 --> 00:08:46.491
Growing up in a place like
this would freak me out.

00:08:47.157 --> 00:08:47.795
Why?

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:52.362
The manicured lawns, the"how
was your day, honey?"...

00:08:52.462 --> 00:08:53.940
I'd blow my brains out.

00:08:55.395 --> 00:08:57.213
There's nothing wrong with normal.

00:08:58.445 --> 00:09:00.380
I'd take our family over normal any day.

00:09:04.598 --> 00:09:06.440
Welcome. Is this the barbecue?

00:09:06.534 --> 00:09:08.774
Yeah, not the best weather, but...

00:09:08.962 --> 00:09:12.704
I'm Larry Pike, the developer here,
and you are? Dean. This is Sam.

00:09:12.968 --> 00:09:14.563
Sam, Dean, good to meet you.

00:09:14.974 --> 00:09:17.578
So, you two are interested
in Oasis Plains? Yes, sir.

00:09:18.106 --> 00:09:18.962
Let me just say

00:09:19.068 --> 00:09:22.552
That we accept homeowners of
any race,religion, color, or...

00:09:23.122 --> 00:09:24.448
Sexual orientation.

00:09:26.078 --> 00:09:27.099
We're brothers.

00:09:27.881 --> 00:09:31.729
Our father is getting on in years, and
we're just looking for a place for him.

00:09:31.823 --> 00:09:32.409
Great,

00:09:32.597 --> 00:09:34.720
Great. Well, seniors are
welcome, too. Come on in.

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:40.889
You said you were the developer?

00:09:41.088 --> 00:09:43.975
18 months ago, I was walking
this valley with my survey team.

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:47.098
There was nothing here but
scrub brush and squirrels,

00:09:47.296 --> 00:09:49.914
And you know what? We built
such a nice place to live

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:52.607
That I actually bought into
it myself. This is our house.

00:09:52.776 --> 00:09:57.012
We're the first family in Oasis
Plains. This is my wife, Joanie.

00:09:57.088 --> 00:09:57.951
Hi, there. Hi,

00:09:57.998 --> 00:09:59.556
Nice to meet you. Sam and Dean.

00:09:59.717 --> 00:10:01.031
Sam. Joannie.

00:10:01.087 --> 00:10:02.814
Tell them how much you
love the place, honey.

00:10:03.217 --> 00:10:06.141
And lie if you have to because
I need to sell some houses.

00:10:07.258 --> 00:10:08.694
Boys, if you'll excuse me.

00:10:09.548 --> 00:10:13.104
Don't let his salesman routine scare
you. This really is a great place to live.

00:10:13.246 --> 00:10:15.132
Hi, I'm Linda Bloom, head of sales.

00:10:15.226 --> 00:10:16.868
And Linda was second to move in.

00:10:16.981 --> 00:10:18.764
She's a very noisy neighbor, though.

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:21.835
She's kidding, of course.

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:24.716
I take it you two are interested
in becoming homeowners.

00:10:25.421 --> 00:10:26.650
Well... Y-Yeah.

00:10:26.653 --> 00:10:31.859
Well, let me just say that we accept
homeowners of any race, religion, color,or...

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:34.252
Sexual orientation.

00:10:34.615 --> 00:10:35.108
Hmm.

00:10:35.272 --> 00:10:35.976
Right.

00:10:36.351 --> 00:10:38.463
Uh, I'm gonna go talk to Larry.

00:10:38.791 --> 00:10:39.659
Okay, honey?

00:10:45.317 --> 00:10:46.877
You have three choices...

00:10:46.995 --> 00:10:49.047
Carpet, hardwood, and tile.

00:10:49.118 --> 00:10:49.845
Whoa,

00:10:50.514 --> 00:10:51.886
Someone likes bugs.

00:10:52.508 --> 00:10:55.523
My son. He's into insects.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:57.758
He's very inquisitive.

00:10:58.509 --> 00:10:59.130
Hmm.

00:10:59.283 --> 00:11:02.509
Who can say no to a steam
shower? I use mine every day.

00:11:02.919 --> 00:11:03.940
Sounds great.

00:11:04.075 --> 00:11:07.336
You also have three different
whirlpool tubs to choose from.

00:11:07.343 --> 00:11:09.522
The hardware for the tubs
include nickel, brass,

00:11:09.574 --> 00:11:12.557
And when you see the kitchens,
you can choose from... Excuse me.

00:11:12.602 --> 00:11:14.021
Um, okay.

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:27.371
Is this yours?

00:11:27.694 --> 00:11:29.351
You gonna tell my dad? I don't know.

00:11:29.541 --> 00:11:30.483
Who's your dad?

00:11:31.188 --> 00:11:31.873
Yeah.

00:11:31.970 --> 00:11:34.610
Larry usually skips me in
the family introductions.

00:11:34.715 --> 00:11:38.281
Ouch. First-Name basis with the
old man... sounds pretty grim.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.252
Well, I'm not exactly brochure material.

00:11:40.572 --> 00:11:42.924
Well, hang in there. It gets
better. Alright? I promise.

00:11:43.458 --> 00:11:44.068
When?

00:11:44.091 --> 00:11:44.713
Matthew!

00:11:53.869 --> 00:11:56.215
I am so sorry about my son and his...

00:11:56.344 --> 00:11:57.834
Pet. It's no bother.

00:11:58.338 --> 00:11:59.394
Excuse us.

00:12:06.612 --> 00:12:07.785
Remind you of somebody?

00:12:12.536 --> 00:12:13.169
Dad?

00:12:14.654 --> 00:12:15.980
Dad never treated us like that.

00:12:16.766 --> 00:12:18.854
Well, dad never treated you
like that. You were perfect.

00:12:18.865 --> 00:12:20.343
He was all over my case.

00:12:22.098 --> 00:12:23.283
You don't remember?

00:12:24.162 --> 00:12:26.555
Maybe he had to raise his voice,
but sometimes you were out of line.

00:12:26.572 --> 00:12:27.294
Right.

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:31.177
Right, like when I said I'd rather
play soccer than learn bow hunting.

00:12:31.371 --> 00:12:32.920
Bow hunting's an important skill.

00:12:34.057 --> 00:12:34.796
Whatever.

00:12:36.181 --> 00:12:37.917
How was your tour?

00:12:38.104 --> 00:12:40.110
It was excellent.I'm ready to buy.

00:12:40.305 --> 00:12:42.112
So you might be onto something.

00:12:42.745 --> 00:12:45.443
Looks like Dustin Burwash wasn't
the first strange death around here.

00:12:45.607 --> 00:12:46.205
What happened?

00:12:46.362 --> 00:12:48.212
About a year ago,
before they broke ground,

00:12:48.272 --> 00:12:50.511
One of Larry's surveyors
dropped dead while on the job.

00:12:50.859 --> 00:12:53.436
Get this... severe allergic
reaction to bee stings.

00:12:53.752 --> 00:12:54.984
More bugs. More bugs.

00:12:57.547 --> 00:12:59.912
I've heard of killer
bees, but killer beetles?

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:01.996
What is it that could
make different bugs attack?

00:13:03.761 --> 00:13:06.683
Well, hauntings sometimes
include bug manifestations.

00:13:06.718 --> 00:13:09.199
Yeah, but I didn't see any
evidence of ghost activity.

00:13:09.349 --> 00:13:10.449
Yeah, me neither.

00:13:12.247 --> 00:13:15.394
Maybe they're being controlled
somehow... by something or someone.

00:13:15.929 --> 00:13:17.172
You mean like "Willard"?

00:13:17.206 --> 00:13:18.792
Yeah, bugs instead of rats.

00:13:20.316 --> 00:13:25.844
There are cases of psychic connections between
people and animals, elementals, telepaths.

00:13:25.856 --> 00:13:27.944
Yeah, that whole Timmy/Lassie thing.

00:13:29.254 --> 00:13:30.532
Larry's kid...

00:13:31.107 --> 00:13:32.362
Bugs for pets.

00:13:32.831 --> 00:13:33.981
Matt? Yeah.

00:13:35.784 --> 00:13:39.186
He did try to scare the realtor with
a tarantula. Think he's our willard?

00:13:39.373 --> 00:13:40.288
I don't know.

00:13:40.347 --> 00:13:41.989
Anything's possible, I guess.

00:13:44.167 --> 00:13:46.055
Ooh, hey, pull over here.

00:13:54.918 --> 00:13:56.314
What are we doing here?

00:14:00.185 --> 00:14:01.768
It's too late to talk to anybody else.

00:14:03.701 --> 00:14:06.117
We're gonna squat in an empty house?

00:14:06.739 --> 00:14:08.693
I want to try the steam shower. Come on.

00:14:09.608 --> 00:14:10.476
Come on!

00:14:38.133 --> 00:14:41.440
Atoko valley county began
mandatory insecticide

00:14:41.478 --> 00:14:44.209
Spraying across a wide
swath of the district today.

00:14:44.249 --> 00:14:49.982
Authorities say the decision to spray was made
because of several recent cases of west nile virus,

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:54.489
Coupled with a dramatic increase in
the mosquito population in some areas.

00:14:54.809 --> 00:14:59.292
Although some residents cite concerns about
the high levels of pesticide being used...

00:15:24.525 --> 00:15:27.763
Aaah! Aaah!

00:15:57.331 --> 00:15:58.570
You ever coming out of there?

00:15:58.730 --> 00:15:59.640
What?!

00:15:59.912 --> 00:16:02.887
Dean, a police call came
in on the scanner. Hold on.

00:16:02.929 --> 00:16:05.800
Someone was found dead three
blocks from here. Come on.

00:16:08.364 --> 00:16:09.838
This shower is awesome.

00:16:10.072 --> 00:16:10.948
Come on.

00:16:39.188 --> 00:16:41.328
Okay, look, I don't know
anything more right now.

00:16:41.375 --> 00:16:42.989
I'll have to call you back.

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:43.843
All right.

00:16:45.251 --> 00:16:46.978
Hello, you're back early.

00:16:46.996 --> 00:16:50.609
Yeah, we wanted to take another look
at the neighborhood. What's going on?

00:16:52.855 --> 00:16:56.308
You guys met Linda
Bloom at the barbecue?

00:16:56.486 --> 00:16:57.322
The realtor.

00:16:57.903 --> 00:16:58.936
Well, she, uh,

00:16:59.831 --> 00:17:01.041
Passed away last night.

00:17:02.496 --> 00:17:03.190
What happened?

00:17:04.553 --> 00:17:05.839
I'm still trying to find out.

00:17:06.402 --> 00:17:08.204
I identified the body for the police.

00:17:09.733 --> 00:17:11.460
I'm sorry. This isn't a good time.

00:17:11.724 --> 00:17:12.325
It's okay.

00:17:12.484 --> 00:17:13.357
Excuse me.

00:17:16.747 --> 00:17:18.052
You know what we have to do, right?

00:17:19.196 --> 00:17:21.786
We got to get in that house.
See if we got a bug problem.

00:17:49.382 --> 00:17:50.902
This looks like the place.

00:18:04.576 --> 00:18:05.468
Spiders.

00:18:06.189 --> 00:18:07.374
From spider boy?

00:18:07.562 --> 00:18:08.312
Matt.

00:18:10.119 --> 00:18:10.905
Maybe.

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:35.633
Isn't his house that way?

00:18:35.692 --> 00:18:36.642
Yep.

00:18:40.149 --> 00:18:41.663
So where's he going?

00:19:07.150 --> 00:19:08.545
Hey, Matt.

00:19:09.355 --> 00:19:10.364
Remember me?

00:19:11.321 --> 00:19:12.294
What are you doing out here?

00:19:12.412 --> 00:19:13.784
We want to talk to you.

00:19:15.368 --> 00:19:16.916
You're not here to buy a house, are you?

00:19:17.956 --> 00:19:18.718
Wait,

00:19:19.539 --> 00:19:20.830
You're not serial killers?

00:19:21.182 --> 00:19:23.281
No, no. No, I think you're safe.

00:19:24.618 --> 00:19:25.651
So, Matt...

00:19:26.798 --> 00:19:28.639
You sure know a lot about insects.

00:19:29.765 --> 00:19:30.340
So?

00:19:31.534 --> 00:19:33.681
Did you hear what happened
to Linda, the realtor?

00:19:35.499 --> 00:19:36.871
I hear she died this morning.

00:19:37.054 --> 00:19:38.133
Mm, that's right.

00:19:38.497 --> 00:19:39.740
Spider bites.

00:19:40.608 --> 00:19:41.359
Matt,

00:19:42.227 --> 00:19:44.526
You tried to scare her with a spider.

00:19:46.153 --> 00:19:46.751
Wait,

00:19:47.443 --> 00:19:48.874
You think I had
something to do with that?

00:19:49.461 --> 00:19:50.528
You tell us.

00:19:51.326 --> 00:19:53.320
That tarantula was a joke.

00:19:53.918 --> 00:19:57.408
Anyway, that wouldn't explain the
bee attack or the gas-Company guy.

00:19:58.768 --> 00:20:00.071
You know about those?

00:20:00.505 --> 00:20:01.877
There is something going on here.

00:20:02.346 --> 00:20:03.437
I don't know what,

00:20:03.539 --> 00:20:04.020
But

00:20:04.443 --> 00:20:06.261
Something's happening with the insects.

00:20:06.530 --> 00:20:08.008
Let me show you something.

00:20:15.856 --> 00:20:18.858
So, if you knew about all this
bug stuff, why not tell your dad?

00:20:18.964 --> 00:20:20.794
Maybe he could clear everybody out.

00:20:20.958 --> 00:20:22.671
Believe me, I've tried, but

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:24.701
Larry doesn't listen to me.

00:20:24.947 --> 00:20:25.604
Why not?

00:20:25.956 --> 00:20:26.941
Mostly?

00:20:27.082 --> 00:20:29.065
He's too disappointed in his freak son.

00:20:30.836 --> 00:20:31.751
I hear ya.

00:20:32.428 --> 00:20:33.202
You do?

00:20:35.501 --> 00:20:36.662
Matt, how old are you?

00:20:36.733 --> 00:20:37.530
16.

00:20:38.868 --> 00:20:41.624
Well, don't sweat it 'cause in two
years something great's gonna happen.

00:20:42.304 --> 00:20:43.617
What? College.

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:46.714
You'll be able to get out of
that house and away from your dad.

00:20:47.301 --> 00:20:49.802
What kind of advice is that? A
kid should stick with his family.

00:20:54.928 --> 00:20:55.961
How much further, Matt?

00:20:56.133 --> 00:20:57.141
We're close.

00:21:18.465 --> 00:21:20.671
I've been keeping track of
the insect population. It's

00:21:20.893 --> 00:21:22.653
Part of an A.P. Science class.

00:21:24.002 --> 00:21:25.269
You two are like peas in a pod.

00:21:27.331 --> 00:21:28.257
What's been happening?

00:21:28.492 --> 00:21:29.313
A lot.

00:21:30.005 --> 00:21:32.527
I mean, from bees to earthworms,

00:21:32.957 --> 00:21:34.083
Beetles...

00:21:34.212 --> 00:21:35.690
You name it. It's

00:21:35.748 --> 00:21:37.543
Like they're congregating here.

00:21:37.590 --> 00:21:38.259
Why?

00:21:38.775 --> 00:21:39.701
I don't know.

00:21:42.326 --> 00:21:43.112
What's that?

00:22:19.937 --> 00:22:21.122
There's something down there.

00:22:27.808 --> 00:22:29.181
Oh, come on.

00:23:19.632 --> 00:23:22.385
So, a bunch of skeletons
in an unmarked grave.

00:23:22.502 --> 00:23:24.473
Yeah, maybe this is a haunting...

00:23:24.602 --> 00:23:25.904
Some pissed-Off spirits,

00:23:26.244 --> 00:23:28.542
Some unfinished business. Yeah, maybe.

00:23:28.624 --> 00:23:30.583
The question is, why bugs

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:31.768
And why now?

00:23:32.225 --> 00:23:33.703
That's two questions.

00:23:35.029 --> 00:23:36.648
So, with that kid back there...

00:23:36.984 --> 00:23:39.471
How could you tell him to just
ditch his family like that?

00:23:39.682 --> 00:23:40.879
Just, uh,

00:23:41.278 --> 00:23:42.943
I know what the kid's going through.

00:23:43.267 --> 00:23:46.751
How about telling him to respect his old
man? How's that for advice? Dean, come on.

00:23:47.455 --> 00:23:49.132
This isn't about his old man.

00:23:49.214 --> 00:23:50.517
You think I didn't respect dad.

00:23:50.634 --> 00:23:51.854
That's what this is about.

00:23:52.998 --> 00:23:54.464
Just forget it. Sorry I brought it up.

00:23:54.523 --> 00:23:55.555
I respected him,

00:23:56.318 --> 00:23:57.702
But no matter what I did,

00:23:57.948 --> 00:23:59.192
It was never good enough.

00:23:59.309 --> 00:24:01.972
What are you saying, that dad
was disappointed in you? Was?

00:24:03.320 --> 00:24:04.153
Is...

00:24:04.623 --> 00:24:06.757
Always has been. Why
would you think that?

00:24:06.804 --> 00:24:08.540
Because I didn't want to bow hunt

00:24:08.709 --> 00:24:11.653
Or hustle pool, because I wanted
to go to school and live my life,

00:24:11.668 --> 00:24:14.052
Which in our whacked-Out
family made me the freak.

00:24:16.127 --> 00:24:18.461
Yeah, you were kind of like the
blond chick in "the munsters."

00:24:19.799 --> 00:24:20.444
Dean,

00:24:21.183 --> 00:24:23.728
You know what most dads are when
their kids score a full ride?

00:24:24.702 --> 00:24:25.417
Proud.

00:24:26.919 --> 00:24:29.112
Most dads don't toss their
kids out of the house.

00:24:30.457 --> 00:24:31.712
I remember that fight.

00:24:32.779 --> 00:24:35.536
In fact, I seem to recall a few choice
phrases coming out of your mouth.

00:24:40.339 --> 00:24:41.114
You know,

00:24:41.630 --> 00:24:44.316
Truth is, when we finally do find dad,

00:24:45.243 --> 00:24:47.272
I don't know if he's
even gonna want to see me.

00:24:49.055 --> 00:24:51.056
Sam, dad was never disappointed in you.

00:24:52.288 --> 00:24:52.980
Never.

00:24:54.247 --> 00:24:55.432
He was scared.

00:24:56.155 --> 00:24:57.328
What are you talking about?

00:24:57.375 --> 00:25:00.038
He was afraid of what could have
happened to you if he wasn't around.

00:25:01.563 --> 00:25:03.263
But even when you two weren't talking,

00:25:04.104 --> 00:25:06.345
He used to swing by
Stanford whenever he could,

00:25:07.107 --> 00:25:08.057
Keep an eye on you,

00:25:08.796 --> 00:25:10.087
Make sure you were safe.

00:25:10.779 --> 00:25:11.717
What?

00:25:13.133 --> 00:25:13.778
Yeah.

00:25:17.943 --> 00:25:19.585
Why didn't he tell me any of that?

00:25:21.549 --> 00:25:24.118
It's a two-Way street, dude. You
could have picked up the phone.

00:25:29.901 --> 00:25:31.736
Come on, we're gonna be
late for our appointment.

00:25:40.053 --> 00:25:41.566
So, you two are students?

00:25:41.991 --> 00:25:43.058
Yeah.

00:25:43.164 --> 00:25:45.416
Yeah, we're in your class.

00:25:45.663 --> 00:25:46.965
Anthro 101.

00:25:47.363 --> 00:25:48.525
Oh, yeah.

00:25:48.595 --> 00:25:49.369
So,

00:25:49.440 --> 00:25:51.410
What about the bones, Professor?

00:25:52.288 --> 00:25:55.045
This is quite an
interesting find you've made.

00:25:55.092 --> 00:25:59.139
I'd say they're 170
years old, give or take.

00:25:59.725 --> 00:26:01.555
The time frame and the geography

00:26:01.574 --> 00:26:03.498
Heavily suggest native american.

00:26:03.944 --> 00:26:07.281
Were there any tribes or
reservations on that land?

00:26:07.363 --> 00:26:10.061
Not according to the historical record,

00:26:10.132 --> 00:26:11.059
But

00:26:11.493 --> 00:26:12.701
The, uh...

00:26:12.748 --> 00:26:16.889
Relocation of native peoples
was quite common at that time.

00:26:17.135 --> 00:26:17.874
Right.

00:26:18.678 --> 00:26:19.312
Well,

00:26:19.828 --> 00:26:21.364
Are there any local legends,

00:26:21.576 --> 00:26:23.793
Oral histories about the area?

00:26:24.778 --> 00:26:25.963
Well...

00:26:26.573 --> 00:26:30.139
You know, there's a
euchee tribe in Sapulpa.

00:26:30.369 --> 00:26:32.128
It's about 60 miles from here.

00:26:33.536 --> 00:26:35.503
Someone out there might know the truth.

00:26:38.612 --> 00:26:39.644
All right.

00:27:26.038 --> 00:27:27.242
Joe Whitetree?

00:27:28.968 --> 00:27:31.983
We'd like to ask you a few
questions, if that's all right.

00:27:32.587 --> 00:27:34.124
We're students from the university.

00:27:34.182 --> 00:27:36.235
No, you're not. You're lying.

00:27:38.276 --> 00:27:39.074
Um,

00:27:39.672 --> 00:27:42.464
The truth is... You know
who starts sentence with

00:27:42.589 --> 00:27:43.669
"Truth is"?

00:27:44.067 --> 00:27:45.064
Liars.

00:27:49.963 --> 00:27:51.722
Have you heard of Oasis Plains?

00:27:51.769 --> 00:27:54.232
It's a housing development
near the Atoka valley.

00:27:56.948 --> 00:27:57.969
I like him.

00:27:58.661 --> 00:27:59.893
He's not a liar.

00:28:00.984 --> 00:28:02.157
I know the area.

00:28:03.541 --> 00:28:05.535
What can you tell us
about the history there?

00:28:05.672 --> 00:28:06.775
Why do you want to know?

00:28:07.444 --> 00:28:08.687
Something...

00:28:09.086 --> 00:28:10.153
Something bad

00:28:11.021 --> 00:28:12.992
Is happening in Oasis Plains.

00:28:13.959 --> 00:28:17.654
We think it might have something to do
with some old bones we found down there...

00:28:18.863 --> 00:28:20.329
Native american bones.

00:28:25.192 --> 00:28:27.503
I'll tell you what my
grandfather told me,

00:28:28.265 --> 00:28:30.107
What his grandfather told him.

00:28:30.857 --> 00:28:32.335
200 years ago,

00:28:32.602 --> 00:28:35.335
A band of my ancestors
lived in that valley.

00:28:36.086 --> 00:28:39.687
One day, the american
calvary came to relocate them.

00:28:42.770 --> 00:28:44.365
They were resistant...

00:28:44.999 --> 00:28:46.665
Calvary impatient.

00:28:48.248 --> 00:28:50.019
As my grandfather put it,

00:28:51.052 --> 00:28:51.887
On a night,

00:28:52.016 --> 00:28:53.060
The moon

00:28:53.388 --> 00:28:54.350
And the sun

00:28:54.631 --> 00:28:56.872
Shared the sky as equals,

00:28:58.162 --> 00:29:00.848
The calvary first raided our village.

00:29:01.466 --> 00:29:02.499
They murdered,

00:29:03.202 --> 00:29:04.035
Raped.

00:29:05.114 --> 00:29:07.470
The next day, the calvary came again,

00:29:07.752 --> 00:29:09.851
And the next and the next.

00:29:10.250 --> 00:29:13.347
And on the sixth night, the
calvary came one last time,

00:29:14.492 --> 00:29:16.510
And by the time the sun rose,

00:29:16.686 --> 00:29:18.820
Every man, woman, and child

00:29:18.891 --> 00:29:20.624
Still in the village

00:29:20.976 --> 00:29:22.008
Was dead.

00:29:26.625 --> 00:29:28.455
They say on the sixth night,

00:29:28.608 --> 00:29:31.212
As the chief of the village lay dying,

00:29:31.564 --> 00:29:33.440
He whispered to the heavens

00:29:34.285 --> 00:29:37.616
That no white man would
ever tarnish this land again.

00:29:38.536 --> 00:29:39.545
Nature

00:29:39.920 --> 00:29:41.105
Would rise up

00:29:41.773 --> 00:29:43.357
And protect the valley,

00:29:43.521 --> 00:29:46.606
And it would bring as many
days of misery and death

00:29:47.177 --> 00:29:48.326
To the white man

00:29:48.983 --> 00:29:51.106
As the calvary had
brought upon his people.

00:29:52.901 --> 00:29:53.992
Insects.

00:29:54.880 --> 00:29:56.299
That sounds like nature to me.

00:29:57.848 --> 00:29:58.915
Six days?

00:29:59.185 --> 00:30:01.285
And on the night of the sixth day,

00:30:02.183 --> 00:30:03.814
None would survive.

00:30:12.243 --> 00:30:14.155
When did the gas-Company man die?

00:30:15.140 --> 00:30:17.744
Let's see, we got here
tuesday, so friday the 20th.

00:30:18.265 --> 00:30:19.168
March 20th.

00:30:20.118 --> 00:30:21.549
That's the spring equinox.

00:30:22.253 --> 00:30:24.611
The night, the sun and the
moon share the sky as equals.

00:30:24.707 --> 00:30:28.542
So every year about this time,
anybody in Oasis Plains is in danger.

00:30:29.211 --> 00:30:32.796
Larry built his neighborhood on cursed land.
And on the sixth night... that's tonight.

00:30:33.125 --> 00:30:36.550
If we don't do something, Larry's
family will be dead by sunrise.

00:30:37.895 --> 00:30:39.303
So how do we break a curse?

00:30:39.631 --> 00:30:40.769
You don't break a curse.

00:30:41.168 --> 00:30:43.350
You get out of its way. We got
to get those people out now.

00:32:01.564 --> 00:32:04.579
Yes, mr. Pike, there's a main-Line
gas leak in your neighborhood.

00:32:04.661 --> 00:32:06.209
God, really? And how big?

00:32:06.315 --> 00:32:09.060
Well, it's fairly extensive.
I don't want to alarm you, but

00:32:09.189 --> 00:32:13.001
We need your family out of the vicinity for
at least 12 hours or so, just to be safe.

00:32:13.139 --> 00:32:14.148
And who is this again?

00:32:14.207 --> 00:32:16.940
Travis Weaver. I work for
Oklahoma gas and power.

00:32:16.987 --> 00:32:17.561
Uh-Huh.

00:32:17.770 --> 00:32:21.606
The problemis I know Travis. He's worked
with us for a year. So who is this?

00:32:22.134 --> 00:32:23.152
Uh...

00:32:24.842 --> 00:32:25.886
Give me the phone.

00:32:34.876 --> 00:32:35.509
Hello?

00:32:35.626 --> 00:32:36.623
Matt, it's Sam.

00:32:36.905 --> 00:32:38.907
Sam, my backyard's
crawling with cockroaches.

00:32:38.908 --> 00:32:42.356
Matt, just listen. You have to get your
family out of that house right now, okay?

00:32:42.648 --> 00:32:43.502
What, why?

00:32:44.390 --> 00:32:45.639
Because something's coming.

00:32:46.296 --> 00:32:47.132
More bugs.

00:32:47.480 --> 00:32:48.738
Yeah, a lot more.

00:32:49.828 --> 00:32:51.922
My dad doesn't listen in
the best of circumstances.

00:32:51.942 --> 00:32:54.889
What am I supposed to tell him?
You got to make him listen, okay?

00:32:55.088 --> 00:32:56.321
Give me the phone. Give me the phone!

00:32:56.532 --> 00:32:59.679
Matt, under no circumstances are you to
tell the truth. He'll just think you're nuts.

00:32:59.808 --> 00:33:02.332
But he's my... Tell him you have
a sharp pain in your right side,

00:33:02.391 --> 00:33:03.952
And you got to go to the hospital, okay?

00:33:04.083 --> 00:33:05.774
Yeah. Yeah, okay.

00:33:09.625 --> 00:33:10.658
"Make him listen."

00:33:11.362 --> 00:33:12.454
What are you thinking?

00:33:24.495 --> 00:33:26.126
Damn it, they're still here. Come on.

00:33:33.957 --> 00:33:36.137
Get off my property
before I call the cops!

00:33:36.184 --> 00:33:37.863
Mr. Pike, listen. Dad,

00:33:38.368 --> 00:33:39.389
They're just trying to help.

00:33:39.436 --> 00:33:40.493
Get in the house!

00:33:41.044 --> 00:33:42.712
Sorry. I told him the truth.

00:33:42.770 --> 00:33:44.602
We had a plan, Matt.
What happened to the plan?

00:33:45.412 --> 00:33:47.020
Look, it's twelve a.M.

00:33:47.161 --> 00:33:48.558
They are coming any minute now.

00:33:48.617 --> 00:33:51.704
You need to get your family
and go before it's too late.

00:33:51.835 --> 00:33:53.830
Oh, yeah, you mean
before the biblical swarm.

00:33:54.006 --> 00:33:56.437
What do you think really
happened to that realtor, huh?

00:33:56.578 --> 00:33:57.975
And the gas-Company guy?

00:33:58.421 --> 00:34:00.240
You don't think something
weird's going on around here?

00:34:00.360 --> 00:34:02.673
Look, I don't know who
you are, but you're crazy.

00:34:02.686 --> 00:34:05.146
You come near my boy or my family again,

00:34:05.243 --> 00:34:06.318
We're gonna have a problem.

00:34:06.363 --> 00:34:09.037
Well, I hate to be a downer, but we got
a problem right now. Dad, they're right.

00:34:09.256 --> 00:34:10.188
We're in danger.

00:34:11.150 --> 00:34:13.163
Matt, get inside now!

00:34:13.539 --> 00:34:14.583
Why won't you listen to me?!

00:34:14.673 --> 00:34:17.043
Because this is crazy!
It doesn't make any sense!

00:34:17.366 --> 00:34:17.900
Look,

00:34:18.160 --> 00:34:19.768
This land is cursed.

00:34:20.106 --> 00:34:23.510
People have died here. Are you gonna
really take that risk with your family?

00:34:23.522 --> 00:34:24.033
Wait.

00:34:26.212 --> 00:34:26.926
You hear it?

00:34:31.346 --> 00:34:32.405
What the hell?

00:34:37.011 --> 00:34:39.077
It's time to go. Larry, get your wife.

00:34:39.798 --> 00:34:40.219
Guys.

00:34:44.447 --> 00:34:45.536
Oh, my god.

00:34:47.616 --> 00:34:48.826
We'll never make it.

00:34:48.878 --> 00:34:50.854
Everybody in the house.
Everybody in the house!

00:34:51.070 --> 00:34:51.739
Let's go!

00:34:56.678 --> 00:34:58.858
Is there anyone else in the
neighborhood? No, it's just us.

00:34:59.497 --> 00:35:00.699
Honey, what's happening?

00:35:01.259 --> 00:35:02.303
What's that noise?

00:35:03.468 --> 00:35:04.437
Call 911.

00:35:05.256 --> 00:35:06.133
Joanie!

00:35:06.389 --> 00:35:07.020
Okay.

00:35:08.275 --> 00:35:09.870
I need towels.

00:35:09.982 --> 00:35:13.242
We got to lock this place up. Come on, doors,
windows, the fireplace, everything. Okay?

00:35:13.941 --> 00:35:14.954
Phones are dead.

00:35:15.035 --> 00:35:16.393
They must have chewed
through the phone lines.

00:35:22.563 --> 00:35:23.597
And the power lines.

00:35:23.838 --> 00:35:24.691
Maybe my cell.

00:35:28.004 --> 00:35:28.946
No signal.

00:35:29.513 --> 00:35:30.487
You won't get one.

00:35:31.220 --> 00:35:32.880
They're blanketing the house.

00:35:49.897 --> 00:35:50.955
So, what do we do now?

00:35:51.682 --> 00:35:52.673
We try to outlast it.

00:35:54.711 --> 00:35:57.469
Hopefully the curse will
end at sunrise. Hopefully?

00:36:20.485 --> 00:36:22.270
Bug spray? Trust me.

00:36:25.229 --> 00:36:25.776
What is that?

00:36:36.281 --> 00:36:37.161
The flue.

00:36:39.975 --> 00:36:41.748
I think everybody needs to get upstairs.

00:36:52.968 --> 00:36:55.226
Everybody upstairs now! Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:36:58.607 --> 00:36:59.956
Quick!

00:37:08.763 --> 00:37:11.248
Okay, Joanie, go, go, go.

00:37:11.285 --> 00:37:12.236
Matt, go.

00:37:13.797 --> 00:37:14.888
Hurry!

00:37:21.666 --> 00:37:22.652
You in? Yeah.

00:37:25.812 --> 00:37:27.574
Come on!

00:37:34.185 --> 00:37:35.582
My god, what's that?!

00:37:41.915 --> 00:37:43.161
Something's eating through the wood.

00:37:44.587 --> 00:37:45.428
Termites.

00:37:49.870 --> 00:37:51.259
All right, everybody get back.

00:37:51.414 --> 00:37:52.856
Get back! Get back!

00:37:52.886 --> 00:37:53.456
Get back!

00:37:54.530 --> 00:37:55.318
Matt.

00:38:57.099 --> 00:38:59.492
Huddle together. Cover your faces.

00:39:10.252 --> 00:39:11.015
Look!

00:40:12.382 --> 00:40:13.328
What, no goodbye?

00:40:13.853 --> 00:40:14.694
Good timing.

00:40:14.807 --> 00:40:16.278
Another hour and we'd have been gone.

00:40:16.834 --> 00:40:17.449
For good?

00:40:18.388 --> 00:40:18.998
Yeah.

00:40:19.051 --> 00:40:22.820
The development's been put on hold while the
government investigates those bones you found,

00:40:23.255 --> 00:40:24.644
But I'm gonna make damn sure

00:40:24.774 --> 00:40:25.908
No one lives here again.

00:40:26.704 --> 00:40:28.152
You don't seem too upset about it.

00:40:29.385 --> 00:40:32.621
Well, this has been the biggest
financial disaster of my career, but,

00:40:34.047 --> 00:40:35.158
Somehow...

00:40:37.059 --> 00:40:38.366
I really don't care.

00:40:53.651 --> 00:40:54.560
What's this?

00:40:54.792 --> 00:40:55.618
I don't know.

00:40:56.827 --> 00:40:57.510
They

00:40:57.788 --> 00:40:59.109
Kind of weird me out now.

00:41:01.690 --> 00:41:03.090
Yeah, I should hope so.

00:41:24.116 --> 00:41:25.197
I want to find dad.

00:41:27.004 --> 00:41:27.807
Yeah, me too.

00:41:29.421 --> 00:41:30.525
Yeah, but I just...

00:41:33.915 --> 00:41:35.341
I want to apologize to him.

00:41:38.884 --> 00:41:39.508
For what?

00:41:42.082 --> 00:41:43.793
All the things I said to him.

00:41:46.651 --> 00:41:48.115
He was just doing the best he could.

00:41:51.483 --> 00:41:53.090
Well, don't worry, we'll find him,

00:41:54.298 --> 00:41:55.752
And you'll apologize,

00:41:56.573 --> 00:41:59.196
And within five minutes, you guys
will beat each other's throats.

00:42:03.274 --> 00:42:05.116
Yeah, probably.

00:42:07.872 --> 00:42:09.444
Let's hit the road. Let's.



